[0m[32mI appreciate the sentiment behind wanting full employment, but I have significant concerns with government guaranteeing jobs. Historically, when government tries to guarantee employment, it creates inefficiencies, waste, and unintended consequences.
[0m[32m
[0m[32mFirst, the free market is far better at matching workers with jobs that suit their skills and interests. When businesses compete for talent, they offer better wages, benefits, and working conditions. Government programs, by contrast, tend to create make-work jobs that don't reflect actual market needs.
[0m[32m
[0m[32mSecond, this would require massive government expansion and spending. Who decides what jobs get created? How do we avoid wasteful projects? This violates the principle of limited government and fiscal responsibility.
