[0m[32mThird, personal responsibility matters. We should encourage people to develop skills, education, and work ethic rather than expecting government to provide. The best path out of poverty is a good job in a growing economy, which comes from economic freedom, not government employment programs.
[0m[32m
[0m[32mInstead, I'd support policies that enable job creation: lower taxes on businesses and individuals, reducing regulations that stifle hiring, protecting property rights, and ensuring quality education so people can compete in the job market. During hardship, temporary targeted assistance is reasonable, but permanent government employment guarantees would ultimately harm economic growth and individual initiative.<|eot_id|>[0m
