[0m[32mI think that's a position worth examining carefully. When government funds arts programs, we're essentially taking tax dollars from working Americans and directing them toward activities that may not align with their values or priorities. The private sector and philanthropic organizations are much better suited to support the arts—they're responsive to what people actually want to fund, and they do it efficiently without bureaucratic overhead.
