[0m[32mThere's also a principle at stake here. The Constitution doesn't enumerate arts funding as a federal responsibility. We've strayed pretty far from limited government when we assume Washington should be the patron of the arts. If communities or states want to support cultural programs, that's their decision to make locally, but it shouldn't be a blanket federal mandate.
[0m[32m
[0m[32mPrivate funding actually creates healthier outcomes too. When artists depend on voluntary contributions and market demand rather than government grants, we get more authentic expression and better alignment between creators and their audiences. We've seen tremendous cultural flourishing throughout history driven by private patronage, not government programs.
