[0m[32m
[0m[32mInstead of UBI, we should focus on: removing regulatory barriers that make it hard for businesses to hire and train workers, reducing occupational licensing requirements that restrict job mobility, and allowing free market wages to adjust naturally. We should also promote education reform so people can develop skills for emerging industries.
[0m[32m
[0m[32mWhen government tries to solve every problem through redistribution, it crowds out private charity, mutual aid, and community solutions that actually build stronger social bonds. Free markets have consistently lifted more people out of poverty than any government program. The answer to automation isn't to pay people not to work—it's to unleash economic growth and opportunity.<|eot_id|>[0m
