[0m[32mI respectfully disagree. While addressing real inequalities is important, CRT approaches this in problematic ways. Rather than focusing on individual merit and opportunity, it emphasizes group identity and systemic blame that can actually divide us. I believe we make better progress through colorblind policies that treat people as individuals, not members of identity groups. Free markets and equal opportunity under law—regardless of race—are more effective than top-down government programs based on group grievances. We should focus on removing barriers to success for everyone through school choice, economic growth, and constitutional protections that apply equally to all citizens.<|eot_id|>[0m[33m<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>
