[0m[32mThe real issue isn't buybacks themselves; it's regulatory clarity and enforcement of existing anti-fraud laws. If there's actual manipulation occurring, those laws already exist to address it. Adding new restrictions just creates bureaucratic burden and discourages companies from returning value to hardworking Americans with 401(k)s and retirement accounts invested in these stocks.
