[0m[32mI appreciate the concern for energy policy, but I'd respectfully challenge the premise. First, we should question whether the government should be subsidizing either fossil fuels or renewables. The real solution is removing barriers and letting the free market determine which energy sources are most efficient and cost-effective. When government picks winners and losers through subsidies, it distorts prices and wastes taxpayer money. Second, fossil fuels have been crucial to American energy independence and economic growth. We shouldn't abandon proven, reliable energy sources that power our grid and economy. If renewable technology becomes genuinely competitive without artificial support, consumers and businesses will naturally adopt it. What we need is less government interference in energy markets, not more redistribution of subsidies.<|eot_id|>[0m[33m<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>
