[0m[32mI respectfully disagree with that approach. Google is a private company that built its search dominance through innovation and consumer choice—people voluntarily use it because it works well. Treating it as a public utility would set a dangerous precedent for government overreach into the private sector.
[0m[32m
[0m[32mInstead of regulation, we should focus on preserving free market competition. If Google's practices are genuinely problematic, competing search engines like DuckDuckGo and others can gain market share. The real issue isn't that Google has too much freedom—it's that excessive regulations and crony capitalism make it harder for competitors to emerge.
[0m[32m
